241
00:12:53,814 --> 00:12:55,774
You implied I'm not a man.

242
00:12:55,775 --> 00:12:58,235
And if I don't seem excited or whatever…

243
00:12:58,736 --> 00:13:01,196
I mean, I really do want to cheer you on,

244
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:03,574
but part of me wants to cheer Leo on too.

245
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:07,202
That's all this is, so, yeah.
Don't think I'm not stoked for you.

246
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,037
Hmm.

247
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:12,875
Oh, I think Ru's back.

248
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:15,044
Ruru?

249
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:16,961
This sucks.

250
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:18,672
- Are you okay?
- Ruru!

251
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:23,134
- What's wrong?
- I seriously can't do this.

252
00:13:23,135 --> 00:13:24,720
Oh, no, are you okay?

253
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:29,307
Ruru, need a tissue? Hand this to her.

254
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:30,935
What's wrong?

255
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:36,232
I seriously don't think I can take it.

256
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:40,945
Mmm.

257
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:44,657
I really don't want
to see Leo anymore today.

258
00:13:47,368 --> 00:13:49,370
- 'Cause it'll make you sad?
- Mmm.

259
00:13:50,746 --> 00:13:52,831
The graduation is day after tomorrow.

260
00:13:52,832 --> 00:13:53,666
Mmm.

261
00:13:56,168 --> 00:13:58,420
Yeah, look,
there's nothing wrong with that.

262
00:14:00,464 --> 00:14:02,967
It's love, everyone gets hurt eventually.

263
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,682
- Wanna go smoke?
- Mmm.

264
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:11,892
Should we?

265
00:14:14,770 --> 00:14:16,939
I just really can't take this.

266
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:21,067
On top of everything,
it must be hard to hear

267
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:23,319
that he was telling everyone
he trusts you and stuff.

268
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:24,487
Yeah, exactly.

269
00:14:24,488 --> 00:14:27,199
Yeah. Plus, Leo said to me himself
that he trusts me.

270
00:14:28,534 --> 00:14:30,286
But I think it's commendable.

271
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:33,955
That you told Leo everything right away.
You didn't even wait.

272
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:35,248
- Yeah.
- Mmm.

273
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:37,208
That's just your true personality.

274
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:38,918
Yeah. That's just you being you.

275
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:40,546
- That's great.
- True.

276
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:43,089
With Kazuma… When it comes to Kazuma,

277
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:45,425
I just feel like I can't fully believe
what he tells me.

278
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:46,427
That makes sense.

279
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:50,931
Like, I've told him I have mixed feelings
about guys who work as hosts.

280
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:54,685
It's a tough situation.

281
00:14:56,687 --> 00:14:58,438
Seriously, I'm so lame.

282
00:14:58,439 --> 00:15:01,024
- You're not lame.
- It's not your fault.

283
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:03,568
Yeah, it's really not.
Seriously, nobody's at fault, really.

284
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:07,405
Leo's not at fault, Kazuma's not at fault,
and you're definitely not.

285
00:15:07,406 --> 00:15:08,908
So you can't blame yourself.

286
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:12,202
- But I get it, though.
- Yo, yo, yo!

287
00:15:12,870 --> 00:15:14,954
- You guys mind if I chat?
- Sure.

288
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:16,539
- Yeah.
- With Ruru.

289
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:18,082
Oh, God.

290
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:20,460
Don't say "Oh, God."
Just relax, it's gonna be fine.

291
00:15:20,461 --> 00:15:22,755
Come on, man, seriously though.

292
00:15:23,714 --> 00:15:25,548
- Sorry. Let's chat.
- All good.

293
00:15:25,549 --> 00:15:26,633
Sure. Let's do it.

294
00:15:26,634 --> 00:15:29,052
- I'm borrowing her.
- Okay.

295
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:31,638
Don't make her cry.

296
00:15:31,639 --> 00:15:32,723
- Oh.
- Okay?

297
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:36,184
- You good?
- Mmm? Mmm-hmm.

298
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:37,645
Read the room, dude.

299
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:42,315
- That was something, huh?
- Tai-chan liked Hikaru for a long time,

300
00:15:42,316 --> 00:15:45,401
but ever since Ruru gave him that talk
in the classroom,

301
00:15:45,402 --> 00:15:46,611
his feelings have shifted.

302
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:49,072
Now he's worshipping
the ground Ruru walks on.

303
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:51,407
There's no more time
to read the room anymore.

304
00:15:51,408 --> 00:15:54,911
They're here to find love,
they have to say how they feel.

305
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:57,747
- As for the agony that Ruru's feeling…
- Yes.

306
00:15:57,748 --> 00:16:00,917
Ms. Awich, what's your take
on her situation? What's going on there?

307
00:16:00,918 --> 00:16:03,920
Well, Leo's words
had to have hit home for her.

308
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:05,296
And now she's taking a beat,

309
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:07,674
so it's possible her feelings
for Leo might grow, right?

310
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:08,967
Definitely possible.

311
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:11,094
After hearing Leo's speech
about the difference

312
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:14,180
between weighing your options
and leading with your feelings…

313
00:16:14,181 --> 00:16:15,098
Being open.

314
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:17,600
I feel like Ruru's gotta be thinking,
"Yeah, that's true."

315
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:18,893
"That's exactly how I see it."

316
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:20,895
- "That makes sense."
- She's getting it.

317
00:16:20,896 --> 00:16:24,565
Ruru has said that she wants
to consider the future

318
00:16:24,566 --> 00:16:26,526
- when it comes to dating.
- Good point.

319
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:30,238
And with Leo, she was having
serious discussions with him, right?

320
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:33,741
Like, "This is what I'm thinking
for the future. This is my dream."

321
00:16:33,742 --> 00:16:35,660
So that's gotta make this harder.

322
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:38,579
Ruru can already visualize
how happy it would make him

323
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:41,040
if she were to choose
to be with him after,

324
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,750
so that makes it more painful.

325
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:46,337
But she really has feelings for Kazu-kun,
so she's like…

326
00:16:46,338 --> 00:16:50,717
And now, she's beating herself up over it,
she's thinking, "Am I a bad person, or…"

327
00:16:50,718 --> 00:16:53,219
- Hence, the too-popular tears?
- Too-popular tears.

328
00:16:53,220 --> 00:16:57,056
How cool is that? Gosh, that must be nice.

329
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:59,267
It kind of sounds
like a Taylor Swift song.

330
00:16:59,268 --> 00:17:02,437
- "Too-Popular Tears."
- The opening song on The Eras Tour.

331
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:03,604
That's true.

332
00:17:03,605 --> 00:17:04,690
Uh, thanks.

333
00:17:05,858 --> 00:17:07,568
So your feelings cooled off?

334
00:17:08,068 --> 00:17:09,194
Yeah, they did.

335
00:17:10,279 --> 00:17:12,905
It wasn't like I got caught up
in the moment or anything.

336
00:17:12,906 --> 00:17:13,741
Mmm.

337
00:17:14,324 --> 00:17:16,993
I did what I did
because I was interested in Kazuma.

338
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:18,953
- That's why.
- Oh, wow.

339
00:17:18,954 --> 00:17:19,913
Okay.

340
00:17:22,624 --> 00:17:26,794
- I keep thinking, "I'm not giving up."
- Oh, God. No, you gotta be kidding.

341
00:17:26,795 --> 00:17:28,756
In my mind, I'm like,
"I'm not gonna lose."

342
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:31,341
- Sorry to put you in a tough spot.
- Well…

343
00:17:33,635 --> 00:17:36,764
Uh, well, like, as of right now…

344
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:40,558
my response is…

345
00:17:40,559 --> 00:17:43,603
my response is
I can't reciprocate those feelings.

346
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:45,646
- <i>Point-blank.</i>
- <i>Clear as it gets.</i>

347
00:17:45,647 --> 00:17:48,859
Also, about what happened yesterday,

348
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:54,406
I just wanna say, the only person I felt
like I needed to come clean to was Leo.

349
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,952
Mmm. Well, that makes sense.

350
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:01,246
Mmm.

351
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:05,708
All I can think is, "Was being
in relationships always this hard?"

352
00:18:05,709 --> 00:18:07,126
Yeah, tell me about it.

353
00:18:07,127 --> 00:18:08,503
- I know, right?
- Mmm.

354
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:10,755
But here,
everyone just says what they mean.

355
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:11,756
- Right?
- Yeah.

356
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:14,760
They say whatever they're feeling
deep down inside, you know?

357
00:18:17,262 --> 00:18:20,264
- Sometimes I wonder if I'm doing that.
- You definitely are.

358
00:18:20,265 --> 00:18:22,726
- You mean that?
- Mmm. Your feelings are clear.

359
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:26,855
Anyway, thanks for telling me.

360
00:18:28,065 --> 00:18:29,650
- Appreciate it.
- Yeah, for sure.

361
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:39,076
Hmm.

362
00:18:40,786 --> 00:18:43,080
Oh, man,
I seriously don't know what to do.

363
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:48,252
- Hey there.
- Oh.

364
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:53,256
What're you doing here?
I'm fine, you know.

365
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:55,466
Wait, no, don't worry,
I'm not here to cheer you up.

366
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:56,592
Okay.

367
00:18:56,593 --> 00:18:58,220
Look, I think that…

368
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:02,265
you should be more careful
about the women you choose.

369
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:03,182
Oh, right.

370
00:19:03,183 --> 00:19:05,518
I'm not saying I know if Ruru
is the right one or not.

371
00:19:05,519 --> 00:19:07,061
- That's not what I'm saying.
- Uh-huh.

372
00:19:07,062 --> 00:19:10,022
But I… I don't think
you need to make a decision yet.

373
00:19:10,023 --> 00:19:12,860
Mmm-hmm. Well,
Maririn did end up telling me

374
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:16,070
how she really feels. Did you know that?

375
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:18,030
- Oh, okay.
- She told you to keep her in mind.

376
00:19:18,031 --> 00:19:19,323
That's right.

377
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:21,451
I've been feeling so uncertain lately,

378
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:24,620
and it felt like her plan
was to come in for the kill.

379
00:19:24,621 --> 00:19:25,705
Mmm.

380
00:19:25,706 --> 00:19:29,625
But, you know, I… I told her
that I wanted to focus on Ruru.

381
00:19:29,626 --> 00:19:32,211
But even after that,
she told me she wasn't going to give up.

382
00:19:32,212 --> 00:19:33,129
Right.

383
00:19:33,130 --> 00:19:35,214
I was like, "Damn,
who knew she was so passionate?"

384
00:19:35,215 --> 00:19:37,008
- I know, right?
- Her heart must be on fire.

385
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:39,177
Exactly. And that's important.

386
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:42,430
I mean, obviously, looks matter,
you gotta go with your gut too.

387
00:19:42,431 --> 00:19:43,265
Mmm.

388
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:47,602
That's all, I just really wanted
to say that to you, Taisei.

389
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:49,146
'Cause I want you to be happy.

390
00:19:53,066 --> 00:19:54,901
- Thank you. That cheered me up.
- Good luck.

391
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:56,068
- Yeah.
- Hang in there.

392
00:19:56,069 --> 00:19:58,237
I'm not giving up. You shouldn't either.

393
00:19:58,238 --> 00:19:59,488
I won't.

394
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:01,033
- Bye-bye.
- See ya.

395
00:20:02,534 --> 00:20:03,577
That felt good.

396
00:20:04,828 --> 00:20:05,870
Man, this is crazy.

397
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:08,332
I've never felt so supported
by my friends before.

398
00:20:10,250 --> 00:20:11,168
I'm going for it.

399
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:13,921
I'm not giving up.

400
00:20:19,259 --> 00:20:22,221
So, did you guys have
a deep conversation or what?

401
00:20:23,639 --> 00:20:25,849
Well, an overnight date is a big deal.

402
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:27,893
We both agreed on that.

403
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:32,814
I'm not budging, though.

404
00:20:33,398 --> 00:20:34,274
I won't.

405
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:40,906
I'm rooting for both of you.

406
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:43,158
Go for it. No regrets, right?

407
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:47,203
- That's all you can do.
- Let's get after it fair and square.

408
00:20:47,204 --> 00:20:48,579
- No regrets.
- Yep.

409
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:51,290
- Things can change so much in one day.
- Mmm.

410
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:53,459
- You never know what's gonna happen.
- Mmm.

411
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:55,294
- Let's give it our all.
- Mmm-hmm.

412
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:56,837
Just do your best.

413
00:20:56,838 --> 00:20:59,132
Fair and square, guys. I'll do the same.

414
00:20:59,633 --> 00:21:02,344
- I'm not letting you win.
- You either, punk.

415
00:21:07,307 --> 00:21:08,976
Whoa.

416
00:21:09,559 --> 00:21:11,019
- Get it!
- Nice.

417
00:21:12,437 --> 00:21:15,022
- He's a beast.
- Why'd you just let him shoot?

418
00:21:15,023 --> 00:21:17,984
<i>Just two days left until your confession,</i>

419
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:20,736
<i>which means alcohol will be available.</i>

420
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:21,862
Yay!

421
00:21:21,863 --> 00:21:23,948
- We're going to have fun.
- Sounds good.

422
00:21:23,949 --> 00:21:25,866
- All right.
- You guys didn't cook?

423
00:21:25,867 --> 00:21:27,952
- We played basketball.
- Where were you?

424
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:29,829
- I made this.
- You serious?

425
00:21:29,830 --> 00:21:31,831
- Don't lie.
- I got some tumblers.

426
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:34,250
We showered after too,
so we can afford to relax now.

427
00:21:34,251 --> 00:21:35,668
- I'm shocked.
- You all did?

428
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:38,296
Maririn, I'll drink
the rest of that beer if you want.

429
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:40,756
- Of course.
- Straight backwash.

430
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:42,633
- Damn right.
- Did your team win?

431
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:44,343
Whoa, no, stop.

432
00:21:44,344 --> 00:21:46,012
- Come at me.
- Slow down.

433
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:48,222
- Where to sit?
- Tai-chan's the king of trash talk.

434
00:21:48,223 --> 00:21:51,309
- Oh, no doubt.
- Fine, guess I'll have beer too.

435
00:21:51,310 --> 00:21:53,602
- He loves to mouth off?
- Only to Bo.

436
00:21:53,603 --> 00:21:56,605
- Here we go…
- Wassup!

437
00:21:56,606 --> 00:21:59,525
- Yay! Woo-hoo!
- Good job, everyone. Cheers.

438
00:21:59,526 --> 00:22:00,819
Wassup, cheers!

439
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:03,237
Mmm!

440
00:22:03,238 --> 00:22:06,198
- Almost done.
- Tomorrow is basically the last day?

441
00:22:06,199 --> 00:22:08,784
- Last chance! It's the last night.
- Tonight is it, right?

442
00:22:08,785 --> 00:22:11,037
- Do they kick us out?
- I'm gonna miss y'all.

443
00:22:11,038 --> 00:22:13,706
- Huh? Oh, right.
- Then, let's go wild tonight.

444
00:22:13,707 --> 00:22:16,834
- <i>Uh, what?</i>
- I'm staying out of trouble.

445
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:18,669
I'm just kidding.

446
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:21,797
- Oh, my heart.
- Someone want the rest of this?

447
00:22:21,798 --> 00:22:23,508
Can I go just a little bit wild?

448
00:22:25,093 --> 00:22:27,387
You never know
what "a little bit" is, though.

449
00:22:27,971 --> 00:22:30,389
- I swear I won't get wasted.
- She's bad news, dude.

450
00:22:30,390 --> 00:22:33,309
<i>Oh, no, how can you possibly
want to drink tonight?</i>

451
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:35,978
- I'm not buying that.
- She's trying to be good.

452
00:22:35,979 --> 00:22:38,565
- Tai-chan, let's talk, okay?
- Sure. Mmm-hmm.

453
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:40,983
<i>Nice, Maririn and Tai-chan.</i>

454
00:22:40,984 --> 00:22:42,902
- <i>Wish them well.</i>
- <i>Good luck.</i>

455
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:44,112
How is it going?

456
00:22:44,613 --> 00:22:47,948
- Well, I had a chat with Ruru today.
- Mmm-hmm.

457
00:22:47,949 --> 00:22:49,326
All right, um…

458
00:22:50,619 --> 00:22:51,745
I'm feeling sad.

459
00:22:52,746 --> 00:22:55,164
What?

460
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:58,710
- Really? You're really feeling sad?
- Mmm, look at me just a little.

461
00:22:59,294 --> 00:23:00,921
I can definitely relate to that.

462
00:23:01,421 --> 00:23:03,255
Romance is really hard, isn't it?

463
00:23:03,256 --> 00:23:04,340
Yeah, but I'm fine.

464
00:23:04,341 --> 00:23:06,759
The way you look at Ruru
doesn't bother me.

465
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:07,969
- Really?
- Mmm.

466
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:09,595
- Wait.
- What?

467
00:23:09,596 --> 00:23:11,847
Why're you looking at me like that?
Did I do something?

468
00:23:11,848 --> 00:23:13,391
No. I wanted to look in your eyes

469
00:23:13,392 --> 00:23:16,060
- 'cause you weren't looking at me.
- I'll look right in your eyes.

470
00:23:16,061 --> 00:23:18,021
- Look at me. Right.
- You got it.

471
00:23:19,398 --> 00:23:20,940
I got it.

472
00:23:20,941 --> 00:23:24,069
You've changed a lot.
You seem a lot more manly now.

473
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:26,696
- Oh, thanks.
- Mmm-hmm.

474
00:23:27,697 --> 00:23:30,951
Right now, it's pretty obvious
that Kazuma is taking the lead.

475
00:23:31,743 --> 00:23:33,577
Then, why don't you go after someone else?

476
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:35,038
- Huh?
- Like me.

477
00:23:35,705 --> 00:23:37,666
You're the only one I said I like.

478
00:23:39,501 --> 00:23:40,877
- Oh, really?
- Uh-huh.

479
00:23:43,713 --> 00:23:46,132
- Can I give you a hug?
- Huh?

480
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:47,384
- What?
- Just a little squeeze?

481
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:50,302
A quick hug, I wanna see how it feels.

482
00:23:50,303 --> 00:23:51,138
Sure.

483
00:23:58,395 --> 00:24:00,813
I mean, I'm hoping this changes your mind.

484
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:02,565
Oh, damn, you smell so good. I'm shook.

485
00:24:02,566 --> 00:24:05,443
- I'm so flustered.
- You smell incredible.

486
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:08,196
The thing is, like,
I know I can make you happy.

487
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:11,907
- That's the thing.
- Yeah.

488
00:24:11,908 --> 00:24:14,660
But, still, it's totally cool,
you should go after who you like.

489
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:15,828
Mmm-hmm. Right.

490
00:24:15,829 --> 00:24:17,746
You never know
what's gonna happen tomorrow.

491
00:24:17,747 --> 00:24:19,290
- True.
- Like, I don't know…

492
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:22,335
who I'm gonna talk to next,
or how my feelings might change.

493
00:24:22,919 --> 00:24:26,005
Don't forget, I would always
take care of you, I promise.

494
00:24:26,006 --> 00:24:27,674
No matter how hard things get.

495
00:24:29,926 --> 00:24:32,136
- I get the message, for sure.
- Mmm-hmm.

496
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:34,055
Oh, that's good to hear.

497
00:24:34,639 --> 00:24:35,806
Think about it.

498
00:24:35,807 --> 00:24:37,976
- I will, no doubt.
- Mmm-hmm.

499
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:40,812
- We only have one more day.
- Yeah.

500
00:24:41,605 --> 00:24:43,439
- Maririn is doing great.
- She is!

501
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:45,650
- She came to seal the deal.
- No question, she's on it.

502
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:49,695
- Like, it's almost too perfect.
- So, you're scared?

503
00:24:49,696 --> 00:24:51,947
No, I'm not scared. More like torn.

504
00:24:51,948 --> 00:24:55,951
I don't feel afraid, I just can't find
anything negative about Bo either.

505
00:24:55,952 --> 00:24:57,369
- Gotcha.
- Believe me.

506
00:24:57,370 --> 00:25:01,165
I've been trying to find something bad,
but I'm coming up empty.

507
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:03,877
What if you did find something? Would you…

508
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:07,755
Honestly, I don't know, but for now…

509
00:25:07,756 --> 00:25:09,716
for now, I mean, it's just you two.

510
00:25:10,217 --> 00:25:12,302
I'm talking with you guys, and that's it.

511
00:25:12,802 --> 00:25:14,888
And it would be bad if I couldn't decide.

512
00:25:15,555 --> 00:25:17,098
Mmm.

513
00:25:18,016 --> 00:25:20,769
Right, okay. So that's what
you've been thinking about.

514
00:25:21,728 --> 00:25:24,104
Bo and you have different approaches
to love, though.

515
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:25,564
- Definitely different.
- Mmm.

516
00:25:25,565 --> 00:25:26,816
- I see that.
- Mmm-hmm.

517
00:25:27,567 --> 00:25:28,485
Yeah, I get it.

518
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:30,278
I understand.

519
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:32,739
So, that's it?

520
00:25:40,789 --> 00:25:43,249
- <i>Look at him smizing.</i>
- <i>He looked handsome.</i>

521
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:44,084
<i>Right?</i>

522
00:25:44,876 --> 00:25:46,460
He is in love.

523
00:25:46,461 --> 00:25:48,671
- He's head-over-heels.
- That's a guy in love.

524
00:25:48,672 --> 00:25:50,965
- Everyone's showing a different side.
- Exactly.

525
00:25:50,966 --> 00:25:52,049
Mmm, yeah.

526
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:53,927
- They're so in love.
- Mmm.

527
00:25:57,931 --> 00:25:58,848
Thanks.

528
00:25:59,724 --> 00:26:00,600
Yeah.

529
00:26:01,309 --> 00:26:02,185
Want one?

530
00:26:04,062 --> 00:26:06,564
- Wait, what? We actually have this flavor?
- Oh, yeah.

531
00:26:06,565 --> 00:26:08,024
- This one.
- Here you go.

532
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:10,359
- We've had this the whole time?
- We have.

533
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:11,777
- Yeah.
- Oh, I didn't know.

534
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:14,489
I thought you might want it,
so I set it aside for you.

535
00:26:15,198 --> 00:26:16,241
What is it?

536
00:26:17,242 --> 00:26:18,326
Green apple.

537
00:26:19,619 --> 00:26:21,454
Honestly, I like you the most.

538
00:26:22,956 --> 00:26:24,749
I thought you might say that.

539
00:26:25,792 --> 00:26:28,294
I haven't decided yet,
so I'm thinking hard now.

540
00:26:28,295 --> 00:26:30,004
I've talked to a lot of people.

541
00:26:30,005 --> 00:26:33,424
I think uncertainty is part of it,
you know, part of being in a relationship.

542
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:34,259
Right.

543
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:36,845
It's all about how you deal with it.

544
00:26:38,888 --> 00:26:43,017
Being with someone,
obviously, it can be incredible.

545
00:26:43,018 --> 00:26:45,936
But you're also seeing
a lot of the other person's flaws.

546
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:48,481
- Yeah.
- So, it's like…

547
00:26:49,357 --> 00:26:51,942
you have to learn
to accept that and love them.

548
00:26:51,943 --> 00:26:55,322
You have to learn how to forgive.
That's how I see it anyway.

549
00:26:56,906 --> 00:26:57,782
Hmm.

550
00:26:59,034 --> 00:27:01,411
- All right.
- I hope tomorrow goes well.

551
00:27:02,162 --> 00:27:03,829
- <i>Whoa!</i>
- <i>Aw.</i>

552
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:05,706
- Bo's making his move too.
- Yep.

553
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:09,001
Everyone is starting to get really honest
and direct with each other.

554
00:27:09,002 --> 00:27:10,419
- You know?
- No kidding.

555
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:13,213
Hikaru is still torn
between Ari and Bo at this point.

556
00:27:13,214 --> 00:27:15,132
- Ari and Bo.
- This is gonna be tough for her.

557
00:27:15,133 --> 00:27:16,884
- Yep.
- A little while ago,

558
00:27:16,885 --> 00:27:20,846
she said something along the lines of,
"Everyone has major flaws," right?

559
00:27:20,847 --> 00:27:22,890
And now she's like,
"They're both perfect."

560
00:27:22,891 --> 00:27:24,725
"That's why I'm so torn."

561
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:27,061
- She's putting herself in a tricky spot.
- That's true.

562
00:27:27,062 --> 00:27:28,812
- It's totally the opposite now.
- For sure.

563
00:27:28,813 --> 00:27:31,982
End of the day,
Bo still has a good chance.

564
00:27:31,983 --> 00:27:34,527
- You think so? Now?
- He might have a chance. Yeah.

565
00:27:35,028 --> 00:27:37,905
- And then there's Ruru and Tai-chan.
- Ruru and Tai-chan, yep.

566
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:40,532
It looked like he was losing hope there,

567
00:27:40,533 --> 00:27:42,451
but thanks to Hikaru's advice,

568
00:27:42,452 --> 00:27:44,244
he's picking himself up
and moving forward.

569
00:27:44,245 --> 00:27:45,162
- Right.
- Yeah.

570
00:27:45,163 --> 00:27:48,123
But then,
Maririn made her move on him just now.

571
00:27:48,124 --> 00:27:49,583
- Yes.
- Wasn't that amazing?

572
00:27:49,584 --> 00:27:52,461
You'd be bowled over.
Imagine someone doing that to you.

573
00:27:52,462 --> 00:27:53,712
Well…

574
00:27:53,713 --> 00:27:55,756
"Imagine someone doing that to you."

575
00:27:55,757 --> 00:27:57,466
I didn't say I was imagining it.

576
00:27:57,467 --> 00:27:59,009
Not personally.

577
00:27:59,010 --> 00:28:01,804
He could've said,
"Imagine them doing that to me."

578
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:05,349
- God. "Me" in there makes it creepy.
- The "me" is off. Be careful.

579
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:08,519
- Don't cancel me. I didn't mean me, folks.
- That's right.

580
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:11,772
So, Tai-chan could seal the deal

581
00:28:11,773 --> 00:28:13,691
- if he chooses this route.
- Right.

582
00:28:13,692 --> 00:28:17,111
I don't know. Tai-chan's always the one
who can't make up his mind.

583
00:28:17,112 --> 00:28:19,405
- Good point.
- The guy always seems

584
00:28:19,406 --> 00:28:21,448
- like he's on the fence.
- He's indecisive.

585
00:28:21,449 --> 00:28:23,701
If he does make a decision,
it breaks down right away.

586
00:28:23,702 --> 00:28:25,828
He lets other people
influence his behavior.

587
00:28:25,829 --> 00:28:27,913
Someone else comes in,
and the wind shifts for him.

588
00:28:27,914 --> 00:28:29,623
Right, he might change his mind again.

589
00:28:29,624 --> 00:28:32,001
He'll go, "Oh, well, I guess…"
in his sweet voice.

590
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:36,297
<i>What are you up to, Assun?</i>

591
00:28:39,968 --> 00:28:41,177
Oh, man.

592
00:28:42,595 --> 00:28:43,847
Oh, hey, Assun.

593
00:28:44,389 --> 00:28:47,225
- Maririn, you want a drink?
- Yeah, let's do it.

594
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:48,976
What are you having?

595
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:51,353
Well, this is basically straight iichiko.

596
00:28:51,354 --> 00:28:53,522
Straight iichiko, on the rocks?

597
00:28:53,523 --> 00:28:56,735
I'll have one. Let's toast.
Can't let you drink alone.

598
00:28:58,403 --> 00:28:59,362
For real, though,

599
00:29:00,071 --> 00:29:02,573
it's just great
that you really got the chance to reflect.

600
00:29:02,574 --> 00:29:06,160
What you said hit me the hardest.
It was seriously amazing.

601
00:29:06,161 --> 00:29:08,662
You're just totally incredible.

602
00:29:08,663 --> 00:29:12,458
- Come here, let me give you a squeeze.
- Aw! You're so cute! What?

603
00:29:12,459 --> 00:29:15,210
Oh, that feels so good.
Careful, I might fall for you.

604
00:29:15,211 --> 00:29:17,422
Well, now I know I'm drunk.

605
00:29:19,174 --> 00:29:20,925
It's been so emotional.

606
00:29:21,509 --> 00:29:22,634
Did you talk a lot?

607
00:29:22,635 --> 00:29:25,053
Yeah, I pretty much told Leo everything.

608
00:29:25,054 --> 00:29:26,765
Whoa. What did he say?

609
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:30,435
- Mmm, he said, "I still like you."
- Oh.

610
00:29:32,145 --> 00:29:35,106
- Yep. That's what he told me.
- How did you feel?

611
00:29:36,024 --> 00:29:38,275
Well, I gotta say, it was kinda touching.

612
00:29:38,276 --> 00:29:39,777
Right, I can imagine.

613
00:29:39,778 --> 00:29:41,570
- Mmm.
- So it hit you hard?

614
00:29:41,571 --> 00:29:44,449
Yeah, just 'cause he's so straightforward.

615
00:29:47,243 --> 00:29:49,578
- And passionate.
- Mmm.

616
00:29:49,579 --> 00:29:50,914
It hasn't changed, though?

617
00:29:51,706 --> 00:29:53,749
- What hasn't?
- The way you feel.

618
00:29:53,750 --> 00:29:55,417
Mmm…

619
00:29:55,418 --> 00:29:56,878
That's a bad sign.

620
00:29:57,587 --> 00:30:00,924
- I mean, it's a question of vibes.
- Uh-huh.

621
00:30:01,508 --> 00:30:03,425
You're not ready yet, are you?

622
00:30:03,426 --> 00:30:05,594
Are we good?

623
00:30:05,595 --> 00:30:07,596
- Still making up my mind.
- Huh? Ah.

624
00:30:07,597 --> 00:30:09,848
Just give me a minute.
I'm right in the middle.

625
00:30:09,849 --> 00:30:10,934
I'm still deciding.

626
00:30:11,476 --> 00:30:14,479
- You're still making up your mind?
- Yeah, of course, I am.

627
00:30:16,564 --> 00:30:18,273
God, look who it is.

628
00:30:18,274 --> 00:30:19,441
You're early.

629
00:30:19,442 --> 00:30:22,362
Ah, shut up.
Come on, Kazuma, it's my turn.

630
00:30:25,406 --> 00:30:26,533
All right, fine.

631
00:30:29,702 --> 00:30:32,831
- Appreciate it.
- No prob. Knock yourself out.

632
00:30:33,456 --> 00:30:36,542
- Man, he seems confident.
- Your face is all red.

633
00:30:36,543 --> 00:30:38,335
- Huh?
- Your face is red.

634
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:39,838
- I'm all good.
- You sure?

635
00:30:41,464 --> 00:30:43,423
- Isn't this amazing?
- Yeah. It's insane.

636
00:30:43,424 --> 00:30:45,593
- God, look at this.
- Beautiful.

637
00:30:47,595 --> 00:30:49,556
This is literally incredible.

638
00:30:53,601 --> 00:30:55,186
- I love the ocean.
- Mmm.

639
00:31:00,692 --> 00:31:01,734
So…

640
00:31:02,861 --> 00:31:04,737
when it comes to you, I'm like…

641
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:08,323
when I started thinking
about the reality of it,

642
00:31:08,324 --> 00:31:11,536
it was hard to imagine it working out,
you know what I mean?

643
00:31:12,036 --> 00:31:14,705
- I told you the reason I feel that way.
- Mmm. Right.

644
00:31:14,706 --> 00:31:17,125
- 'Cause we'd have to face the reality…
- Mmm.

645
00:31:18,751 --> 00:31:20,712
- …of a long-distance relationship.
- Mmm.

646
00:31:23,381 --> 00:31:24,506
Hmm.

647
00:31:24,507 --> 00:31:27,510
And that would just be
too big a price to pay.

648
00:31:29,178 --> 00:31:31,347
But I've already decided
I'm going to Tokyo.

649
00:31:31,848 --> 00:31:34,767
- Yeah, yeah, I know. I understand.
- Mmm. Mmm.

650
00:31:36,102 --> 00:31:37,644
But, then, that means…

651
00:31:37,645 --> 00:31:40,982
If moving to Tokyo means
you have to give up on your dreams,

652
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:43,317
I don't want you to throw that away,

653
00:31:43,318 --> 00:31:46,237
because I'm the same,
I'm chasing my dreams too.

654
00:31:47,030 --> 00:31:49,032
No, it's not gonna ruin my dreams.

655
00:31:50,074 --> 00:31:52,660
Not if I do it for you.
It wouldn't ruin it.

656
00:31:53,953 --> 00:31:55,830
If it's for you, I'll move.

657
00:31:56,581 --> 00:31:58,081
Otherwise, I don't know.

658
00:31:58,082 --> 00:31:59,459
Mmm.

659
00:32:00,501 --> 00:32:04,421
You have no idea how hard it was for me
to hear that you said you trusted me.

660
00:32:04,422 --> 00:32:05,465
Yeah.

661
00:32:06,382 --> 00:32:08,133
Well, I do trust you.

662
00:32:08,134 --> 00:32:10,469
- Even if he's the one--
- No, stop saying you trust me.

663
00:32:10,470 --> 00:32:11,304
Why?

664
00:32:12,263 --> 00:32:13,848
It makes this harder for me.

665
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:20,772
I'm ready to commit…

666
00:32:21,981 --> 00:32:23,024
to you for life.

667
00:32:26,027 --> 00:32:27,070
I'll protect you.

668
00:32:28,071 --> 00:32:29,572
I'll help you stop cheating.

669
00:32:30,156 --> 00:32:32,617
I'll help you through any problems
you may have.

670
00:32:33,368 --> 00:32:34,702
I'll do anything for you.

671
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:39,540
I want you to let me carry your burdens.

672
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:47,131
That's what a real man does.

673
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:57,933
- I have to say, Leo's really amazing.
- I know.

674
00:32:57,934 --> 00:33:00,852
- So consistent. Rock solid.
- He's determined.

675
00:33:00,853 --> 00:33:03,981
- So true. It's incredible.
- I know, right?

676
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:06,566
Now even Kazuma is feeling it.
He's like, "What?"

677
00:33:06,567 --> 00:33:10,028
- "Haven't you made up your mind yet?"
- You could tell he was shocked.

678
00:33:10,029 --> 00:33:11,488
- He was so confident.
- True.

679
00:33:11,489 --> 00:33:15,743
My guess is that Kazu-kun is really used
to women throwing themselves at him.

680
00:33:16,536 --> 00:33:19,371
Especially when he comes on
that strong, you know?

681
00:33:19,372 --> 00:33:22,874
- He puts himself in that position a lot.
- He's been popular before.

682
00:33:22,875 --> 00:33:26,421
And Ruru hasn't told Kazuma
that she likes him, has she?

683
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:28,797
- Has she?
- Oh, wait, maybe she hasn't.

684
00:33:28,798 --> 00:33:31,299
- Yeah, maybe not.
- That's fascinating.

685
00:33:31,300 --> 00:33:34,803
At this stage, uh, he's like,
"Wait a minute. What's happening?"

686
00:33:34,804 --> 00:33:36,179
"She's not telling me."

687
00:33:36,180 --> 00:33:38,390
I bet Kazu-kun has never met
a woman like Ruru before.

688
00:33:38,391 --> 00:33:40,058
- That's my theory.
- This is new.

689
00:33:40,059 --> 00:33:42,853
If that's the case,
this is probably confusing for him.

690
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:45,772
- Like, "This is me we're talking about."
- "This is me, come on."

691
00:33:45,773 --> 00:33:48,025
"Wait, how could this be happening
to a guy like me?"

692
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:49,026
- Wow.
- Right.

693
00:33:49,027 --> 00:33:50,278
Interesting.

694
00:33:52,321 --> 00:33:53,698
It doesn't show up, right?

695
00:33:54,407 --> 00:33:56,992
Here, try writing in this spot.
This grey section.

696
00:33:56,993 --> 00:33:59,244
- Oh, here?
- Yep, right there.

697
00:33:59,245 --> 00:34:00,579
BADLY IN LOVE 2

698
00:34:00,580 --> 00:34:02,289
We have so many with doodles on them.

699
00:34:02,290 --> 00:34:04,082
CHEERS - THREE-MAN CELL
AT THE BAR!

700
00:34:04,083 --> 00:34:05,542
Looks like we need to take more.

701
00:34:05,543 --> 00:34:07,754
MARIRIN - LOVEY-DOVEY
WE LOVE MR. HENTONA - WE'RE DATING

702
00:34:09,338 --> 00:34:10,339
That's me.

703
00:34:11,966 --> 00:34:14,342
2026 - 2 DAYS UNTIL CONFESSION
BO

704
00:34:14,343 --> 00:34:17,013
- You're in a lot of these.
- I guess so.

705
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:19,389
I'm always trying to be myself.

706
00:34:19,390 --> 00:34:20,974
- Mmm-hmm.
- No matter where I am.

707
00:34:20,975 --> 00:34:23,561
- Yeah, I'm getting used to it now.
- Mmm.

708
00:34:24,937 --> 00:34:27,314
- You're used to me?
- Yeah.

709
00:34:27,315 --> 00:34:29,649
Well, I've been saying it to everybody,

710
00:34:29,650 --> 00:34:32,694
like, we all need to hang out
after we finish this.

711
00:34:32,695 --> 00:34:34,112
- You know?
- Nah, I'll pass.

712
00:34:34,113 --> 00:34:37,074
What? You're the worst.

713
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:39,910
- Show me around if I go to Fukuoka.
- I'm not going out.

714
00:34:39,911 --> 00:34:40,828
Why not?

715
00:34:41,579 --> 00:34:42,871
Because I'm a hermit.

716
00:34:42,872 --> 00:34:43,955
Do it for me.

717
00:34:43,956 --> 00:34:46,291
- Okay, fine.
- But you have to be enthusiastic.

718
00:34:46,292 --> 00:34:49,044
- Nah, I'll be grumbling.
- You…

719
00:34:49,045 --> 00:34:50,462
<i>They're a good match.</i>

720
00:34:50,463 --> 00:34:53,465
- <i>They're great together.</i>
- <i>They're perfect for each other.</i>

721
00:34:53,466 --> 00:34:55,759
You're so kind.
I really like that about you.

722
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,345
- Think so?
- Mmm.

723
00:34:58,137 --> 00:35:00,597
Well, I really try
not to hurt people, you know?

724
00:35:00,598 --> 00:35:02,599
<i>Boy, he's softened up a lot, hasn't he?</i>

725
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,102
<i>I know, right?</i>

726
00:35:05,728 --> 00:35:09,022
Bo's personality
is so, like, big and warm.

727
00:35:09,023 --> 00:35:13,068
<i>I guess I can only really go
on our time together yesterday and today,</i>

728
00:35:13,069 --> 00:35:16,530
<i>but I feel like we're getting
a lot closer really quickly.</i>

729
00:35:16,531 --> 00:35:18,115
<i>He loves to play tricks on me.</i>

730
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:20,910
<i>He's like
a cute little elementary school boy.</i>

731
00:35:21,410 --> 00:35:23,995
<i>He'll like… He'll tap me on the shoulder,</i>

732
00:35:23,996 --> 00:35:26,790
<i>and when I turn around,
he'll go "Rah!" and scare me.</i>

733
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:31,129
<i>And I'm like, "Ah! What's wrong with you?"
He just has such a playful energy.</i>

734
00:35:32,296 --> 00:35:34,089
I feel like, of all the guys here,

735
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:36,508
he'd be the best to be
in a relationship with.

736
00:35:36,509 --> 00:35:38,260
But he likes Hikaru.

737
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:40,429
I mean, I could see that from the get-go.

738
00:35:42,348 --> 00:35:45,934
The funny thing is, the fact
that he's so consistent about his feelings

739
00:35:45,935 --> 00:35:48,061
is part of what makes Bo so charming.

740
00:35:48,062 --> 00:35:50,772
I had no idea he was like that,
'cause we didn't talk for so long.

741
00:35:50,773 --> 00:35:51,690
<i>True.</i>

742
00:35:51,691 --> 00:35:53,483
<i>She really likes him, doesn't she?</i>

743
00:35:53,484 --> 00:35:56,319
- So you're conflicted?
- Yeah, it's complicated.

744
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:57,530
I can imagine.

745
00:35:58,281 --> 00:36:01,950
Obviously, it's my fault for not having
my mind made up yet about this.

746
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:04,411
- I'm being so lame. I feel like I suck.
- No, you're not.

747
00:36:04,412 --> 00:36:05,912
- You're cool.
- No, I'm being lame.

748
00:36:05,913 --> 00:36:06,913
- Stop it.
- No joke.

749
00:36:06,914 --> 00:36:10,500
But if you say you're lame, I don't have
to listen to that lecture you gave me.

750
00:36:10,501 --> 00:36:13,421
- I thought you wouldn't listen.
- That's not true.

751
00:36:14,255 --> 00:36:17,966
It was you and Assun, and you guys
just sat down and said it like it is.

752
00:36:17,967 --> 00:36:20,386
- Yeah.
- You told me to do the right thing.

753
00:36:21,095 --> 00:36:23,598
You were like,
"Don't you hurt our Maririn."

754
00:36:25,766 --> 00:36:27,475
And I was like, "They're right."

755
00:36:27,476 --> 00:36:31,313
It's funny, I've never gotten any advice
or anything from women before,

756
00:36:31,314 --> 00:36:33,232
- or been lectured like that.
- Mmm.

757
00:36:34,275 --> 00:36:37,319
I want to thank you for that,
'cause it helped me change.

758
00:36:37,320 --> 00:36:40,155
I owe you two a lot
for helping me be a better man.

759
00:36:40,156 --> 00:36:42,700
- Mmm, mmm.
- Mmm. So, yeah.

760
00:36:45,453 --> 00:36:48,663
I just wanted to thank you for all that.
I'm so glad we met.

761
00:36:48,664 --> 00:36:52,126
And thank you for making me
fall in love with you this hard.

762
00:36:52,752 --> 00:36:54,878
Mmm.

763
00:36:54,879 --> 00:36:57,255
Well, yeah, I really feel your gratitude.

764
00:36:57,256 --> 00:36:58,673
- That's important.
- Really.

765
00:36:58,674 --> 00:37:00,927
- Accepting a thank-you is hard for me.
- Mmm.

766
00:37:01,510 --> 00:37:04,429
So, I don't know
who's gonna end up with who.

767
00:37:04,430 --> 00:37:05,347
Right.

768
00:37:05,348 --> 00:37:09,518
I don't know where any of us
will go from here, but…

769
00:37:10,895 --> 00:37:14,231
but the friends I met here,
I'm gonna see them again somewhere.

770
00:37:14,232 --> 00:37:16,359
- Mmm.
- Mmm-hmm.

771
00:37:17,526 --> 00:37:19,778
I feel this isn't gonna be the end for us.

772
00:37:19,779 --> 00:37:20,613
I know.

773
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:23,156
- Wanna meet up after we graduate?
- For sure.

774
00:37:23,157 --> 00:37:24,407
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

775
00:37:24,408 --> 00:37:26,869
- I wanna meet up with everyone.
- I feel that.

776
00:37:27,578 --> 00:37:30,497
Kazuma or Leo, whoever you choose…

777
00:37:30,498 --> 00:37:31,581
Mmm.

778
00:37:31,582 --> 00:37:33,876
I promise I'll support you as a friend.

779
00:37:34,835 --> 00:37:36,420
- Don't cry.
- I'm sorry.

780
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:40,590
- I've been crying a lot.
- No, it's okay. It's okay.

781
00:37:40,591 --> 00:37:41,968
- Thank you.
- Mmm.

782
00:37:42,593 --> 00:37:43,636
Of course.

783
00:37:48,474 --> 00:37:50,517
- Good morning!
- What's good, everyone?

784
00:37:50,518 --> 00:37:52,727
- Morning, morning, morning!
- Morning.

785
00:37:52,728 --> 00:37:54,729
- He's so loud.
- Gotta start the day right.

786
00:37:54,730 --> 00:37:57,066
Good morning, wassup? Whoo!

787
00:37:57,650 --> 00:38:00,360
I feel like I barely slept.

788
00:38:00,361 --> 00:38:03,071
- He's a little too relaxed.
- Too what?

789
00:38:03,072 --> 00:38:05,240
- Excuse me.
- "Relaxed."

790
00:38:05,241 --> 00:38:07,535
- Will you stop?
- What's happened now?

791
00:38:08,244 --> 00:38:10,620
- Hang on.
- Sorry to interrupt,

792
00:38:10,621 --> 00:38:13,206
but there's one other thing
I need to tell you all.

793
00:38:13,207 --> 00:38:15,293
- Are you guys ready?
- <i>Wait a minute, what?</i>

794
00:38:15,835 --> 00:38:17,085
So…

795
00:38:17,086 --> 00:38:19,796
Assun, do you remember
what you did late last night?

796
00:38:19,797 --> 00:38:20,631
Huh?

797
00:38:21,465 --> 00:38:22,591
<i>Wait, no way.</i>

798
00:38:26,971 --> 00:38:28,014
No, I don't.

799
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:35,313
What?

800
00:38:38,065 --> 00:38:40,568
Wait, hold on.
Isn't the next episode the last one?

801
00:38:41,610 --> 00:38:44,572
- Yes.
- So, what's gonna happen?
